{
  "description": "Sycamore labelled T1 in sketch plan. Proposed Works:\rA crown reduction of approximately 2 metres to the existing canopy, reducing the overall height and spread of the tree whilst retaining its natural shape, form and structure.\rReason for Proposed Works:\rThe proposed crown reduction is intended as a proactive maintenance measure to manage the overall size and growth of the tree within its surroundings.\rThe works will help prevent the tree from becoming excessively large for its location, whilst maintaining a balanced and aesthetically pleasing crown. The reduction will also help preserve the visual amenity of the surrounding area and ensure the tree remains in keeping with the character and appearance of the local environment.\rThe proposed works are intended to maintain the tree?s overall health, condition and structural balance, whilst allowing it to continue contributing positively to the streetscape and local amenity.\rAll works will be undertaken in accordance with good arboricultural practice, following BS3998:2010 (Tree Work ? Recommendations), ensuring the tree?s natural form and long-term health are retained.",
